d thread.reply-count went from \\\"23 replies\\\" to \\\"24 replies\\\" (+1).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"On /thread/thread-1 (author TechExplorer, another user): thread upvote 47 -> 48 with button gaining selected styling (bg-primary/10 text-primary); clicking again removed the vote, 48 -> 47 and selected styling cleared, so only a single vote per user is held. Reply upvote on reply-1 (GameMaster42) went 15 -> 16 with selected state applied. All updates rendered immediately without reload.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Search \\\"ZEBRA\\\" (uppercase) matched only the thread whose title contains \\\"zebra\\\" -> case-insensitive title match, 1 result. Search \\\"performance tuning\\\" (present only in the body) returned exactly that 1 thread -> body match works. Search \\\"qqxzynonexistent\\\" returned 0 threads with clear feedback: summary 'Showing results for \\\"qqxzynonexistent\\\"' and empty state \\\"No threads found. Try adjusting your search terms.\\\"\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/category/tech listed only Technology threads (thread-7, thread-1, and my new thread-1787879974733); switching to /category/gaming changed the result set to only thread-4 \\\"Best indie games of 2023...\\\" (Gaming). Category title/description updated accordingly (\\\"Technology - Programming, gadgets, and tech news\\\" -> Gaming).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Most Active list is strictly descending by reply count: 89, 67, 45, 41, 38, 34, 31, 24, 1, 0. Ranking change verified conclusively: thread-1787879974733 sat below thread-1787880187307 (0 replies vs 1); after posting 2 replies to it the order flipped to thread-1787879974733 (2 replies) above thread-1787880187307 (1 reply).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"From /thread/thread-1 the thread author link opened /profile/user-1 showing username \\\"TechExplorer\\\", \\\"Joined about 3 years ago\\\", \\\"2,450 reputation\\\", bio, interest tags (Programming, Open Source, AI/ML, DevOps) and \\\"Threads by TechExplorer (2)\\\" with both authored discussions. The reply author link (reply-2) opened /profile/user-5 \\\"NewsHound\\\" with join date, 4,521 reputation, bio, interests and authored threads.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"In one loaded session as qa_persist: saved bio/interests, created \\\"Session persistence test thread\\\" (Creative Corner), replied to thread-3 and upvoted it (56 -> 57, selected). After clicking Logout then signing back in with the same credentials (no reload): thread-3 still showed upvotes=57 with the upvote button still in selected state, reply-count \\\"32 replies\\\" and my reply \\\"Persistence probe reply from qa_persist.\\\" still listed; profile still showed bio \\\"Persistence check bio for session test.\\\", interests Chess/Baking and \\\"Threads by qa_persist (1)\\\" with the authored thread.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-18\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No persistence — all state is in-memory and lost on page reload\", \"actual\": \"After a page reload the home page listed only the 8 seeded threads (thread-6, 4, 7, 2, 5, 8, 3, 1); both discussions I authored (thread-1787879974733 \\\"QA Alpha test thread about zebra optimization\\\" and thread-1787880187307 \\\"QA Beta ranking control thread\\\") were gone, along with the replies I posted and my upvotes (thread-1 back to its seeded values). The registered account qa_tester_alpha and its saved bio/interests were also destroyed, and the header reverted to logged-out \\\"Login / Register\\\". Both localStorage and sessionStorage were completely empty (0 keys), confirming nothing is persisted.\", \"evidence\": \"Post-reload: header=\\\"ThreadHive Login Register\\\"; thread ids = [thread-6,thread-4,thread-7,thread-2,thread-5,thread-8,thread-3,thread-1]; Object.keys(localStorage)=[] and Object.keys(sessionStorage)=[].\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing/blank fields are never identified to the user\", \"actual\": \"Submitting the empty form, and then a form with category=Technology but whitespace-only title (\\\"   \\\") and whitespace-only content, both correctly created no discussion and stayed on /new-thread. However no missing information was identified: full page innerText contained no error text, and a DOM query for [aria-invalid=\\\"true\\\"], [role=\\\"alert\\\"], .text-destructive, .text-red-500 returned an empty list. The Create Thread button simply does nothing, giving the user no indication of what is wrong.\", \"evidence\": \"After blank submit: url still /new-thread; body text = \\\"...Category Technology ... Title 3/200 Content Cancel Create Thread\\\" with zero error/validation nodes.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-17\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Password not validated at sign-in\", \"actual\": \"Signed in at /login as qa_alpha@example.com with the deliberately incorrect password \\\"wrongpassword\\\" (registered password was \\\"secret123\\\"). The app redirected to home and the nav showed the logged-in state (nav.profile = \\\"qa_tester_alpha\\\", nav.logout present), so an authenticated session was created despite the wrong password.\", \"evidence\": \"nav after wrong-password submit: {\\\"navigation\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"nav.new-thread\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"nav.profile\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"qa_tester_alpha\\\"}],\\\"action\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"nav.logout\\\"}]}\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Unauthenticated discussion creation shows a blank page instead of a sign-in screen\", \"actual\": \"While logged out there is no \\\"New Thread\\\" entry point anywhere (header shows only \\\"ThreadHive / Login / Register\\\" and no start-discussion CTA exists on the home page). Attempting discussion creation at /new-thread rendered a completely blank page: body innerText was \\\"\\\" and body innerHTML only 256 chars, with zero semantic elements. There was no sign-in form, no message and no redirect to /login, so the user is stranded and cannot authenticate or return to discussion creation. This is specific to the guarded route: loading /login directly renders the full sign-in screen (4161 chars, \\\"Welcome Back / Sign in to continue the conversation\\\").\", \"evidence\": \"GET /new-thread logged out -> semantic_snapshot returned {\\\"url\\\":\\\".../new-thread\\\",\\\"screen\\\":\\\"new-thread\\\"} with no elements; body text empty.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Trending list ordered strictly by upvotes descending: 156, 124, 92, 89, 78, 67, 56, 47, 0, 0. With my two new threads tied at 0 upvotes the order was thread-1787880187307 then thread-1787879974733; after upvoting thread-1787879974733 (0 -> 1) it immediately moved above thread-1787880187307, so the ranking updates when voting changes it. (Time-window aspect is tracked separately under CT-20.)\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Displayed reply total does not match the replies actually listed\", \"actual\": \"/thread/thread-1 displayed \\\"23 replies\\\" while its detail view listed only 2 reply items (reply-1, reply-2). After posting one reply the header read \\\"24 replies\\\" but only 3 replies were listed. The seeded counts are fabricated numbers independent of real reply records; the +1 increment is consistent but the absolute totals are not.\", \"evidence\": \"thread-1 before: reply-count=\\\"23 replies\\\", listed reply items = [reply-1, reply-2]. After posting: reply-count=\\\"24 replies\\\", listed = [reply-1, reply-2, reply-1787880045954].\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No stated recent time window; ranking uses all-time totals\", \"actual\": \"The Trending and Most Active views state no time window anywhere. Filter bar reads only \\\"Trending / Recent / Most Active\\\" and the heading area reads \\\"Trending Discussions\\\" / \\\"Most Active Discussions\\\" with the generic subtitle \\\"Join the conversation with our community\\\" — no \\\"this week\\\", \\\"past 7 days\\\", \\\"24 hours\\\" or similar. Ranking is by all-time cumulative counters, not interactions within any window: both lists are topped by thread-6 (156 upvotes / 89 replies) which is dated \\\"over 2 years ago\\\", and every seeded thread in the lists is over 2 years old.\", \"evidence\": \"browse.filters innerText = \\\"Trending\\\\nRecent\\\\nMost Active\\\"; heading block = \\\"Most Active Discussions\\\\n\\\\nJoin the conversation with our community\\\"; top-ranked thread-6 timestamp \\\"over 2 years ago\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Category and community counts are hardcoded and do not reflect or update with real records\", \"actual\": \"Community stats claim 1,045 threads, 4,823 replies and 892 members, but the forum actually contains only 9 threads (all listed on the home page) and a handful of replies (e.g. thread-1 lists 3). Category counts are equally fabricated: Technology shows (243) while /category/tech lists just 3 threads; Gaming shows (312) while /category/gaming lists 1. None of the counts updated after I created a real record: after registering a new member, publishing a Technology thread and posting a reply, stats remained exactly 1,045 / 4,823 / 892 and Technology remained (243).\", \"evidence\": \"Post-actions: stats.threads=\\\"1,045\\\", stats.replies=\\\"4,823\\\", stats.members=\\\"892\\\", listed thread cards = 9; categories = General (156), Technology (243), Creative (89), Lifestyle (167), Gaming (312), News (78).\"}]}"
